{
    "task_id": "web_word_sheet_arxiv_QA_04",
    "instruction": "I want to analyze the full LLaMA 2 model family. Search 'Llama 2: Open Foundation and Fine-Tuned Chat Models' on arXiv, then find: (1) all four model sizes in the family (in billions of parameters), and (2) how many billion tokens all variants were trained on. Write all five values in Word. Then in the spreadsheet, enter the four model sizes from smallest to largest in A1 through A4, and training tokens in billions in A5. In column B: create a label showing the model size range in B1, compute the tokens-per-parameter ratio for the largest model (round to 1 decimal place) in B2, label it 'Overtrained' if that ratio exceeds 20 otherwise 'Undertrained' in B3, compute the geometric mean of the smallest and largest model sizes (round to 2 decimal places) in B4, compute the cube root of the ratio between the largest and smallest model (round to 2 decimal places) in B5, and compute the base-10 logarithm of the training token count (round to 1 decimal place) in B6.",
